      'Draw keeps the canvas first, with brush, smudge, eraser, selection, transform, layers and colour close by. Tap More tools for Vector, Bucket fill, adjustments and Reference without expanding the main toolbar. On narrow screens swipe the pinned tool row; More tools stays at its edge. Tap the active Brush or Vector again for its brush library. Animate keeps its own setup, with Flipbook for drawing frames and Clips for arranging them.',
      'Workspace in the bottom bar (or Menu → App settings → Workspace layout) lets you pin extra tools, reorder them with Move up/down or dragging, dock the toolbar at the top/left/right, move brush controls, and show tool labels. Each mode remembers its own arrangement. Apply settings keeps the draft; Cancel discards it. Restore the selected mode’s class defaults, then Apply, to recover its starting layout. These choices also save in student profiles on this device and never change artwork.',
